= Genomics — Simple =

Genomics studies genomes at large scale: all or much of an organism's DNA, including genes, regulatory regions, variation, and interactions. It is broader than sequencing the genome and is not the same thing as genetics.

'''Important boundary:''' genomics ≠ genetics.

